1
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:23,750
So the design splits in two.

2
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:28,250
A cheap monitor that watches every night and uses no AI.

3
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:32,750
And an agent that wakes up only when there is something worth explaining.

4
00:02:28,717 --> 00:02:33,217
Every night the system runs the same twenty one steps.

5
00:02:33,217 --> 00:02:37,717
The screen you are looking at is the real record of one of them.

6
00:03:59,650 --> 00:04:04,150
A night is not a clock window. It is the sleep your watch actually recorded.

7
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:08,650
Sleep from midnight to seven would miss a shift worker entirely.

8
00:04:08,650 --> 00:04:13,150
The number that matters is the lowest sustained heart rate while you slept.

9
00:07:16,983 --> 00:07:21,483
This is a real person, over a month.

10
00:07:21,483 --> 00:07:25,983
Green means this night looked like your normal.

11
00:07:25,983 --> 00:07:30,483
Nothing has happened yet, and nothing needed to be said.

12
00:08:21,033 --> 00:08:25,533
A hard training session late in the evening.

13
00:08:25,533 --> 00:08:30,033
It barely moves the night, and nothing is said.

14
00:08:30,033 --> 00:08:34,533
A heavier drinking night than usual. Now the night is amber.

15
00:08:34,533 --> 00:08:39,033
Amber does not raise an alarm. That is a decision, and it was measured.

16
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:44,800
The first red night.

17
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:49,300
No alert. An alarm needs two raised nights in a row.

18
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:53,800
The person mentions feeling dizzy, without being asked.

19
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:58,300
Dizziness is recorded, and on its own it raises nothing.

20
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:02,800
There is no trustworthy figure for how long dizziness must last to matter.

21
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:07,300
So the system tracks it and does not pretend to know.

22
00:10:47,583 --> 00:10:52,083
And the line it works against was not chosen by anybody.

23
00:10:52,083 --> 00:10:56,583
Missing an illness is set at nine times worse than a false alarm.

24
00:10:56,583 --> 00:11:01,083
One divided by one plus nine gives ten percent. The threshold falls out of that.

25
00:12:01,583 --> 00:12:06,083
Second red night in a row. Now an investigation opens.

26
00:12:06,083 --> 00:12:10,583
This is the first time in eleven days the AI has done anything.

27
00:12:10,583 --> 00:12:15,083
It weighs twelve possible causes, and it asks one question.

28
00:12:15,083 --> 00:12:19,583
Watch the list of causes rearrange after a single answer.

29
00:12:19,583 --> 00:12:24,083
Every reply the model produces is checked against a strict shape before anything acts on it.

30
00:12:48,833 --> 00:12:51,833
The question arrives on Telegram, and can be answered from there.

31
00:12:51,833 --> 00:12:54,833
The investigation is then parked, and picked up days later where it left off.

32
00:12:54,833 --> 00:12:57,833
It remembers across the waiting, which is what makes it an agent and not a chat window.

33
00:13:47,133 --> 00:13:51,633
Every clinical sentence has to quote words that appear in a real source.

34
00:13:51,633 --> 00:13:56,133
If it cannot, the sentence is removed, or flagged in amber as unsourced.

35
00:15:06,917 --> 00:15:11,417
Fever reported yesterday. Vomiting reported today.

36
00:15:11,417 --> 00:15:15,917
Neither one alone changes anything.

37
00:15:15,917 --> 00:15:20,417
Together they do, and the system now reads them together.

38
00:15:20,417 --> 00:15:24,917
See a doctor today. Decided by code, before the AI was asked.

39
00:16:43,683 --> 00:16:48,183
Every step, every source, every decision, with the time it happened.

40
00:16:48,183 --> 00:16:52,683
Each entry is sealed with a fingerprint of the entry before it.

41
00:16:52,683 --> 00:16:57,183
Change any one of them and the chain stops matching.

42
00:17:27,233 --> 00:17:31,733
The heart rate settles. The person says the fever has gone.

43
00:17:31,733 --> 00:17:36,233
The investigation does not close.

44
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:45,875
The AI drafted its conclusion and stopped to have it checked.

45
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:50,250
It does not get to publish that on its own.

46
00:18:50,250 --> 00:18:54,625
The next day the fever returns, and the person rejects the draft.

47
00:18:54,625 --> 00:18:59,000
The investigation stays open, because a person said so.

48
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:03,375
Days later, recovered, they read the final one and approve it.

49
00:19:03,375 --> 00:19:07,750
It never worked out what caused this, and it closes saying exactly that.

50
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:12,125
Not an all clear. It does not have one to give.

51
00:19:12,125 --> 00:19:16,500
And it says so out loud. An investigation that ends in silence reads as reassurance.

52
00:20:08,117 --> 00:20:12,617
Chest pain is not handled by spotting the words chest pain.

53
00:20:12,617 --> 00:20:17,117
The AI asks five specific questions. Then code, not the AI, scores the answers.

54
00:21:23,733 --> 00:21:28,233
And when the picture is one the rule was never tested on,

55
00:21:28,233 --> 00:21:32,733
such as pain right now with sweating or fainting,

56
00:21:32,733 --> 00:21:37,233
the rule is not allowed to run at all. That is an emergency, with no questions.

57
00:22:23,950 --> 00:22:28,450
The AI is now pointed at an address that does not answer.

58
00:22:28,450 --> 00:22:32,950
The monitor still scores the night. The safety checks still run.

59
00:22:32,950 --> 00:22:37,450
The question still goes out, in plain prepared words.

60
00:22:37,450 --> 00:22:41,950
The screen says so, rather than pretending.

61
00:22:41,950 --> 00:22:46,450
An outage in the AI must never be able to hide somebody's illness.
